text:
Everyone is arguing about AI sandbox pricing, but they're not even comparing the same thing.

@boatdotdev sells a whole VM at a flat hourly rate, $0.018 an hour, so you can predict the bill.

@Agent37HQ sells minutes and sleeps the box down to just disk, so an agent that mostly sits idle costs less.

@vercel Sandbox only bills CPU while your code is actually running, which makes sense because an agent spends most of its life waiting on an LLM response.

@e2b sells the trust layer, a real microVM per session, for running code you do not trust.

@daytonaio sells pause and fork, so you can freeze a running machine and clone it into twenty copies.

And there are about 30 of these on one public benchmark alone, which probably makes it the most competitive space in infra right now. Feels a lot like the vector DB rush in 2023, when everyone shipped roughly the same thing and then spent a year posting benchmarks at each other 😂
